# Line endings. The repo is LF throughout, and this is what keeps it that way on
# every platform: Git for Windows defaults to `core.autocrlf=true`, which would
# otherwise materialize every text file as CRLF in a Windows working tree. The
# `mixed-line-ending --fix=lf` pre-commit hook is not a substitute — it runs on
# files being committed, after checkout has already decided what is on disk.
#
# `text=auto` leaves Git's own binary detection in charge, so images and fonts
# are untouched; the explicit `binary` lines below are belt-and-braces for the
# formats where a stray "looks like text" heuristic would corrupt the file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Vendored fonts and print-resolution guide figures — byte-for-byte upstream.
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.pdf  binary

# C64 payloads: SID tunes, PRGs, cartridge images, raw memory dumps. These
# carry $0d/$0a bytes as data, not as line terminators.
*.sid binary
*.prg binary
*.crt binary
*.d64 binary
*.bin binary
